    "body": "Implements the CSS rule parser specified in ADR-009 (`docs/decisions/009-css-parser.md`).\n\n## Background\n\nADR-009 decided that we implement a stylesheet parser ourselves in `renderer/css/stylesheet.{hpp,cpp}`, rather than using lexbor's CSS module. This mirrors the reasoning in ADR-007 and ADR-008: our cascade needs our own typed `Declaration`/`Rule` model, which we will extend with computed values in Phase 3.\n\n## Scope\n\n### New files\n\n- `src/renderer/css/stylesheet.hpp` — public types\n- `src/renderer/css/stylesheet.cpp` — parser implementation\n- `tests/test_stylesheet.cpp` — unit tests\n\n### Public API\n\n`Stylesheet::parse(std::string_view) -> Stylesheet`\n\nNever fails. Malformed rules and declarations are silently skipped (per CSS 2.1 error handling). Always returns a valid (possibly empty) `Stylesheet`.\n\n### Data model\n\n- `Declaration { std::string property; std::string value; bool important; }`\n- `Rule { SelectorList selectors; std::vector<Declaration> declarations; }`\n- `Stylesheet { std::vector<Rule> rules; }`\n\n### Behavior (from ADR-009's table)\n\n- `h1 { color: red; }` → 1 rule, 1 declaration\n- `h1 {}` → 1 rule, empty declarations (valid)\n- `h1 { color: red }` → 1 rule (trailing semicolon optional)\n- `h1 { color: red; broken ; font-size: 20px; }` → 1 rule, 2 declarations (broken skipped)\n- `{ color: red; }` → 0 rules (empty selector invalid)\n- `h1 { color }` → 0 declarations (missing colon)\n- `h1 { color: red } h2 { color: blue }` → 2 rules\n- `h1 { color: red !important }` → 1 declaration with `important = true`\n- `/* comment */ h1 { color: red; }` → 1 rule, comment stripped\n- `h1 { color: red` → 0 rules (unclosed brace)\n\n### Deferred (per ADR-009)\n\n- At-rules: `@media`, `@import`, `@font-face`, `@supports`\n- Custom properties (`--x`), `var()`, `calc()`, `rgb()`\n- Shorthand expansion (raw value string preserved; expansion happens at cascade time)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `renderer/css/stylesheet.{hpp,cpp}` compile into `honeybee_lib`\n- [ ] Tests in `tests/test_stylesheet.cpp` cover every row of ADR-009's behavior table\n- [ ] Malformed rules and declarations are skipped, not fatal\n- [ ] `!important` sets `Declaration::important = true`\n- [ ] Comments (`/* ... */`) are stripped before parsing\n- [ ] `grep -rl \"lexbor/\" src/` still returns exactly `src/renderer/html/convert.cpp`\n- [ ] `SelectorList::parse` is called, not reimplemented\n- [ ] `renderer::dom` untouched — this is text-in, structure-out\n- [ ] CI green\n\n## Two-commit plan\n\n- **Commit 1 — rule skeleton**: `Stylesheet::parse` finds rule boundaries, delegates to `SelectorList::parse`, handles malformed-rule recovery. Declarations empty.\n- **Commit 2 — declarations**: split on `;` and `:`, trim whitespace, detect `!important`, strip `/* */` comments, handle malformed-declaration recovery.\n\nEach commit independently reviewable; CI isolates any failure to a specific half.\n\n## Refs\n\n- ADR-009: `docs/decisions/009-css-parser.md`\n- ADR-008: `docs/decisions/008-css-selectors.md`\n- ADR-007: `docs/decisions/007-dom-ownership.md`\n",
